{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short -- docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md; wc -l docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md; sed -n '1,30p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md\"","aggregated_output":"?? docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md\n     327 docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md\n---\ndescription: Alpha-canonical de Bruijn projection of the named Universal AST\n---\n\n# DE BRUIJN PROJECTION OF THE UNIVERSAL AST\n\nStatus: design and implementation plan. This document defines a new\ncompilation-layer projection. It does not amend the Universal AST, its walker,\nor the semantic VM.\n\nThe compilation path is:\n\n```\nYang -> named Universal AST -> de Bruijn projection -> projected form\n                                  |\n                                  +-> canonical fingerprint\n```\n\nThe named form remains the bijective, stored and queryable representation. The\nprojected form is a derived value used for alpha-equivalence and deduplication.\nNeither form replaces the other.\n\n## 1. Architectural position and invariants\n\nThe projection is an interpreter over plain AST datoms. It is not a VM pass and\ndoes not execute literals, primitives, stream operations, continuations, or\neffects. It reads the named form and emits another plain-data stream.\n\nIt obeys the following rules.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
