{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-20 17:34:56 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-21 00:34:56 +07 (Indochina Time)\n\nAuthored [yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md).\n\nThe design specifies:\n\n- A pure scope-aware de Bruijn projection for every node emitted by `yin.vm`.\n- Canonical projected d5 tuples under `:yin.db/*`, with lambda arities, bound depth indices, preserved free names, and canonicalized references.\n- Deterministic traversal, shared-node context handling, cycle rejection, and host-independent SHA-256 fingerprint encoding.\n- A stream-to-stream forward adapter positioned after Yang AST emission and before projected storage.\n- Separate consumers for named versus projected forms.\n- Phased implementation plan D0–D6, completion criteria, and a comprehensive test matrix.\n- Explicit non-changes to the AST, walker, semantic VM, linearizer, named storage, `dao.stream`, `dao.lease`, and waitset.\n\nOpen questions concern parameter depth convention, shared-node duplication, unordered literals, projected storage vocabulary, fingerprint versioning, and source-to-projected provenance retention."}}
